        {
            "id": "filesystem-intro",
            "type": "screen",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "className": "alert",
                    "text": "SECTION: FILE SYSTEM SCREENS"
                },
                "",
                "A screen with \"type\": \"filesystem\" renders a three-region file",
                "browser inside its own chrome (a title bar over a framed viewport).",
                "It is one self-contained view: selecting things updates it in place",
                "and never changes screens.",
                "",
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "className": "system",
                    "text": "[STRUCTURE]"
                },
                "- the screen's link elements are the FOLDERS (left column)",
                "- a folder's target screen supplies the FILE list (top right):",
                "    - that target's own link elements are the files, or",
                "    - if the target has no links, the target itself is one file",
                "- the selected file's target supplies the CONTENT (bottom right)",
                "",
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "className": "system",
                    "text": "[PROPERTIES]"
                },
                "- headerTitle (on the file system screen): title bar text",
                "- title (on a content screen): the name shown in the file list",
                "",
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "className": "system",
                    "text": "[BEHAVIOUR]"
                },
                "- info file: if a folder's target has text as well as links, that",
                "  text becomes a file named after the folder, listed first",
                "- buttons: a folder or file whose target is an ARRAY navigates or",
                "  runs an action instead of opening content, e.g.",
                "  \"target\": [ { \"type\": \"action\", \"action\": \"back\" } ]",
                "- back links: a link pointing back at the file system screen itself",
                "  is hidden, so a converted screen's \"< BACK\" link is not listed",
                "- content: file bodies render the same elements a normal screen",
                "  does, including class names, markdown, images, and prompts",
                "",
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "className": "system",
                    "text": "[WHOLE-SCRIPT CHROME]"
                },
                "Setting config.terminalType to \"alien\" wraps every screen in the",
                "same chrome, so classic screens sit inside the framed viewport too.",
                "It is not required: a \"filesystem\" screen brings its own chrome.",
                "",
                {
                    "type": "link",
                    "text": "> OPEN THE LIVE FILE SYSTEM",
                    "target": "file-system-demo"
                },
                {
                    "type": "link",
                    "text": "> KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS",
                    "target": "keybinds"
                },
                {
                    "type": "link",
                    "text": "> TABLE OF CONTENTS",
                    "target": "hub"
                }
            ]
        },
